## Tier 2 — Graph-structural ideas

Deterministic computations over the reference/call graph.

### 4. Cycle / knot detection (strongly connected components)

Surface groups of symbols that form circular dependencies — units of behavior wearing several names that cannot be changed independently. Warns against local fixes inside a knot; identifies external entry points where a fix can legitimately land.

### 5. Fan-in / fan-out ranking

Per-symbol dependency counts, ideally split src/test. High fan-in = load-bearing (edit is a de facto API change); high fan-out = orchestrator. Cheapest idea in the catalog; likely delivered as annotation (see #3) rather than a command.

### 6. Blast radius (backward/forward cones)

Transitive reachability from a symbol: forward cone = everything this change could affect; backward cone = every possible origin of a value (provenance/precedence debugging). Only useful bounded and with join points highlighted — raw cones explode.

### 7. Chokepoints, dominators, mandatory paths

Symbols every path between subsystems (or from an entry point) must cross — central validation, guards, invariant boundaries. Standard compiler algorithms applied at repo scale.

### 8. Layering / depth map

Distance-from-entry-points as an architectural layering signal; edges that skip many layers flagged as suspicious.

